    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36-a2">

                <pb facs="0137" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg41"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 60.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr. Chester.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inquiry has been made at this legation by
                    the Department of State as to a certain Ignatz Gutman, a naturalized citizen of
                    the United States, who was born in Rosenau, in the district Gomor, in Hungary.
                    The friends of Mr. Gutman have informed the Secretary of State that he has been
                    arrested and is now made to perform military duty in the Twenty-fifth Regiment
                    of the Hungarian army, stationed at Losoncz, in the district of Neograd.</p>
                <p>I shall thank you to inform me whether you have ever heard of this man; and, if
                    so, whether he is now under arrest, as has been reported. If you have no
                    knowledge of him, please take such steps as you may be able, to discover the
                    facts of the case, and report to me as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne Tower.</hi>
                            </item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank D. Chester</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">United States Consul, Budapest.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
